{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef long double ld;\n\nstatic inline ld absv(ld x) { return x < 0 ? -x : x; }\n\nvoid try_first(ll q, ll d, ld target, ld &bestErr, ll &bestNum, ll &bestDen) {\n    ld e = absv((ld)q / d - target);\n    if (e < bestErr || (e == bestErr && (d < bestDen || (d == bestDen && q < bestNum)))) {\n        bestErr = e;\n        bestDen = d;\n        bestNum = q;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid try_second(ll q, ll d, ld target, ld &bestErr, ll &bestNum, ll &bestDen) {\n    ld e = absv((ld)(q + 1) / d - target);\n    if (e < bestErr || (e == bestNum && (d < bestDen || (d == bestDen && q + 1 < bestNum)))) {\n        bestErr = e;\n        bestDen = d;\n        bestNum = q + 1;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid try_third(ll q, ll d, ld target, ld &bestErr, ll &bestNum, ll &bestDen) {\n    ld e = absv((ld)(q - 1) / d - target);\n    if (e < bestErr || (e == bestNum && (d < bestDen || (d == bestDen && q + 1 < bestNum)))) {\n        bestErr = e;\n        bestDen = d;\n        bestNum = q - 1;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll a, b, n;\n    cin >> a >> b >> n;\n\n    ld target = (ld)a / b;\n    ld bestErr = 1000000000.0L;\n    ll bestNum = 0, bestDen = 0;\n\n    for (ll d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        ll q = (a * d) / b;\n        try_first(q, d, target, bestErr, bestNum, bestDen);\n        try_second(q, d, target, bestErr, bestNum, bestDen);\n        if (q == 0) continue;\n        try_third(q, d, target, bestErr, bestNum, bestDen);\n    }\n\n    cout << bestNum << \"/\" << bestDen << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef try_first(q, d, target, best):\n    e = abs(q / d - target)\n    if e < best[0] or (e == best[0] and (d < best[2] or (d == best[2] and q < best[1]))):\n        best[0] = e\n        best[1] = q\n        best[2] = d\n\ndef try_second(q, d, target, best):\n    e = abs((q + 1) / d - target)\n    # Note: original C++ code uses bestNum (best[1]) instead of bestErr (best[0]) in the equality check\n    if e < best[0] or (e == best[1] and (d < best[2] or (d == best[2] and q + 1 < best[1]))):\n        best[0] = e\n        best[1] = q + 1\n        best[2] = d\n\ndef try_third(q, d, target, best):\n    e = abs((q - 1) / d - target)\n    # Note: original C++ code uses bestNum (best[1]) and also incorrectly uses q+1 instead of q-1\n    if e < best[0] or (e == best[1] and (d < best[2] or (d == best[2] and q + 1 < best[1]))):\n        best[0] = e\n        best[1] = q - 1\n        best[2] = d\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    a, b, n = map(int, data[:3])\n    target = a / b\n    best = [1e9, 0, 0]  # [bestErr, bestNum, bestDen]\n\n    for d in range(1, n + 1):\n        q = (a * d) // b  # integer division, assuming positive numbers\n        try_first(q, d, target, best)\n        try_second(q, d, target, best)\n        if q == 0:\n            continue\n        try_third(q, d, target, best)\n\n    print